# Response headers for everything Pages serves statically.
#
# Cloudflare already sets `x-content-type-options: nosniff` and a referrer
# policy; this pins those and adds the three that were missing — a content
# policy, transport security, and a refusal to be framed.
#
# NOTHING HERE SETS Cache-Control. The gate rewrites every gated response to
# `private, no-store` + `Vary: Cookie` (see functions/api/_middleware.ts), and
# that is the invariant standing between a hundred people's records and a shared
# edge cache. A blanket cache header in this file is exactly how it would be
# undone by accident.
#
# `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` is likewise left alone on static assets. It
# is Pages' own default, it applies to files any visitor may already GET, and
# the module script and stylesheet are requested with `crossorigin` — removing
# it risks breaking the load for no security gain. What matters is that it is
# NOT on the gated routes, and it is not.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; media-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=(), interest-cohort=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
